# etude-3343: bind gate verdicts to reviewed bytes and permit same-name recapture

Profile dev-claude, run `etude-3343-dev-claude`. Base commit 42d3593. Audit findings A01 (P1) and A15 (P2) from etude-jhnk.

## Requirements and acceptance criteria

| # | Requirement | Acceptance evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| R1 | `etude gate` rejects a supplied artifact whose SHA-256 differs from the latest captured output for the stage's produced role, before any check, seat, scratch creation or ref write. | Engine test: mismatch returns error, zero check and seat invocations, run ref commit unchanged. Fresh-binary CLI reproduction of A01 fails closed. |
| R2 | The recorded `reviewed_stages[0].artifact` digest is the digest of the bytes every seat actually reviewed. | Equal-bytes engine test passes and the recorded digest equals SHA-256 of the request artifact. |
| R3 | The mismatch error names run, stage, role, expected and supplied digests and the recapture command shape. | Error-string assertions in the engine test and CLI reproduction output. |
| R4 | Appending a stage under an already gated name with different output keeps the run valid; the earlier gate's digest still validates. | Manifest validation unit test with duplicate names and CLI flow capture A, gate blocked, same-name capture B, gate pass. |
| R5 | A reviewed reference with a digest validates only when some same-named stage occurrence carries that digest as output, log or input. A digest present only on a differently named stage is rejected. Digestless references keep name-existence semantics. | Manifest validation unit tests plus JSON roundtrip with duplicate names and the old digest. |
| R6 | Prior-attempt evidence and reviewed-ref consumers keep selecting the stage occurrence whose output matches the recorded digest, not the latest by name. | Existing `stageByReviewedRef` tests in `internal/liverun/gate_test.go` stay green; no change to that function. |
| R7 | Docs describe the binding, the recapture path and the validation rule. | `docs/gates.md`, `docs/capture.md`, `docs/development.md` edits; `make docs-check` and `make docs-reality` pass. |

## Invariants

- Binding hash is `sha256.Sum256` of the raw artifact slice, lowercase hex, identical to `artifactstore.hashBytes`. No trimming, normalization or prompt-envelope bytes participate. A trailing-newline difference is a mismatch.
- Every stage output already carries a valid SHA-256 (`validateArtifactRef` at `internal/runmanifest/manifest.go:797`), so there is no digestless output branch. The gate never skips binding.
- The mismatch check happens after `latestStageForRole` and before tier resolution, `nextPhaseRound`, prompt build, `MkdirAll(ScratchDir)`, checks and seats. Nothing is written on mismatch.
- The bytes hashed are the same `req.Artifact` slice passed to `buildGatePrompt`. No second read.
- Manifest validation keeps all existing identifier and digest-format checks. Gate ordering relative to stages is unchanged: all stages are indexed before any gate is validated, so no temporal or forward-reference policy is introduced.
- Stage names are never rewritten. No `.rN` auto-naming, no occurrence index, no sequence field, no schema version bump, no migration. Repeated identical digests under the same name remain ambiguous for producer metadata; that is a pre-existing schema limit and is out of scope.
- The generic validator stays output/log/input aware. Only the supervised gate binds to output specifically.

## Design

### 1. `internal/liverun/gate_once.go`

After resolving `reviewed`:

```go
supplied := hex.EncodeToString(sha256sum(req.Artifact))
if supplied != reviewed.Output.Artifact {
    return GateOutcome{}, fmt.Errorf("%w: run %s stage %q output role %q is %s but the supplied artifact is %s; recapture it first (etude capture %s --run %s --expect append --output %s=<artifact-path>, where <artifact-path> is the file given to gate --artifact) then rerun this gate",
        ErrArtifactMismatch, req.RunID, reviewed.Name, req.Stage.Produces, reviewed.Output.Artifact, supplied, reviewed.Name, req.RunID, req.Stage.Produces)
}
```

Add `var ErrArtifactMismatch = errors.New("gate artifact does not match captured output")` next to `ErrNoReviewableStage`. Imports `crypto/sha256` and `encoding/hex`. Nothing else in the function moves; the check sits at line 115, immediately after the `ErrNoReviewableStage` return. The recorded `ReviewedStages[0].Artifact` stays `reviewed.Output.Artifact`, which is now provably equal to the supplied digest.

The CLI in `internal/cli/gate.go` needs no new request field. `runGateCommand` already holds `cfg.artifactPath`; wrap `ErrArtifactMismatch` there only if the placeholder text is judged unhelpful. Default: leave the CLI untouched, the engine message is already actionable. Reviewer may request the CLI substitution; it is a two-line `errors.Is` wrap.

### 2. `internal/runmanifest/manifest.go`

Change the validation index at line 312 from `map[string]Stage` to `map[string][]Stage`, appending every occurrence. `validateGate` takes the new type. Reference resolution:

```go
occurrences, ok := stageIndex[ref.Stage]   // missing name: unchanged error
if ref.Artifact != "" {
    // format check unchanged
    found := false
    for _, s := range occurrences { if stageHasArtifact(s, ref.Artifact) { found = true; break } }
    if !found { return existing "not found on stage ... output or inputs" error }
}
```

Error text keeps the existing prefix so current tests and docs stay valid; append "(any stage named ...)" only if a reviewer asks. `stageHasArtifact` is unchanged.

### 3. Consumers checked, no change

- `internal/liverun/gate.go:498` `stageByReviewedRef` already matches name and output digest walking backwards. Unchanged.
- `internal/cli/run.go:410` prints refs verbatim. Unchanged.
- `internal/cli/capture.go` `capture-gate` serializes refs and relies on `Validate`. Gains the relaxed rule for free.
- `latestStageForRole` (engine.go:76) still picks the newest occurrence for a role, which is the intended recapture semantics: after a corrected capture the next gate reviews the newest bytes.

### 4. Tests

`internal/liverun/gate_once_test.go`

- Introduce `const seededGateArtifact = "the artifact under review\n"` used by `seedGateRun`. Existing tests pass `[]byte("x")` in roughly twenty places (lines 169 to 996); those must switch to `[]byte(seededGateArtifact)` or they will now fail with the mismatch. Tests that assert an earlier failure (missing run, missing role, read_checkout, resolver-required errors) may keep `"x"` where the failure precedes the binding check; only the ones that expect seats or checks to run change. Docs-stage tests (`gateOnceDocsStage`) seed their own bytes and follow the same rule.
- `TestGateStageRejectsArtifactMismatchBeforeChecksAndSeats`: seed run, pass different bytes, assert `errors.Is(err, ErrArtifactMismatch)`, message contains run id, stage name, role, both digests and `etude capture verify --run r1 --expect append --output verify=`; check runner and seat resolver counters are zero; `ScratchDir` was not created; `Store.Resolve` returns the same commit as before.
- Newline cases in one table test: seeded without trailing newline and supplied identical passes; seeded with newline and supplied identical passes; seeded with newline and supplied without newline rejects; and the reverse rejects.
- `TestGateStageRecordsDigestOfReviewedBytes`: equal bytes pass and `Gates[0].ReviewedStages[0].Artifact == hex(sha256(req.Artifact))`.

`internal/runmanifest/manifest_test.go`

- `TestValidateAcceptsReviewedRefOnEarlierSameNameStage`: two stages named `review` with outputs A then B; gate references `review` with digest A; `Validate` passes; JSON roundtrip through `ParseJSON` preserves both stages and the digest.
- Same-name earlier occurrence matched via input digest and via log digest both validate.
- Digest present only on a differently named stage is rejected with the existing "not found on stage" error.
- Digest of a nonexistent artifact and malformed digest remain rejected (extend the existing `TestValidateGateRejects` table where a case is missing).
- Digestless reference to an existing name passes; to a missing name fails (already covered, confirm).

`internal/cli/capture_test.go` (or a new `gate_test.go` in `internal/cli`)

- End-to-end in-process flow using `execute(...)` with a workflow named `gated` whose stage `review` produces `review` and gates on a one-seat inline tier, and a registry seat invoking a shell script that writes `{"verdict":"block","required":["fix"]}` on the first call and `{"verdict":"go"}` afterwards (the script keys off a counter file in the temp dir). Steps: capture `review` with file A; gate blocked, ref gains gate `review.r1` citing digest A; edit the file to B; gate without recapture fails with `ErrArtifactMismatch` and the ref is unchanged; capture `review` again with `--expect append`; gate passes as `review.r2` citing digest B. Assert both stage occurrences exist with their original bytes readable from the ref and both gate digests are intact. Registry and seat-script wiring copies the pattern at `internal/cli/run_test.go:1141-1233`.

`internal/liverun/gate_test.go` prior-attempt evidence: confirm an existing test selects the older occurrence by digest; add one only if none does.

### 5. Documentation

- `docs/gates.md` line 66 onward: state that a reviewed-stage digest must match the output, log or an input of any stage occurrence with that name, so recapturing under the same name keeps earlier gates valid. Add a short "Binding" paragraph: `etude gate` hashes the supplied file and refuses when it differs from the latest captured output for the role, with the recapture command.
- `docs/capture.md` Capturing review gates section: one paragraph on recapturing changed bytes under the same stage name with `--expect append` and that earlier gates keep referencing the earlier occurrence by digest.
- `docs/development.md` Capture and review: the sentence "Always recapture changed bytes before a review" gains the fact that `etude gate` enforces it.
- `docs/plans/dogfood/supervisor-runbook.md` line 140: mark the `<phase>.r2` rename convention as optional now that same-name recapture is supported; a one-line note, not a rewrite.
- `docs/cli/etude_gate.md` is generated. Extend the `Long` text in `internal/cli/gate.go` with one sentence on the byte binding and regenerate with `make docs`.
- `CHANGELOG.md`: add an Unreleased entry under Fixed for A01 and A15.

## Failure cases

| Case | Behaviour |
| --- | --- |
| Supplied file differs from latest captured output | `ErrArtifactMismatch`, exit non-zero, nothing written, no seat cost. |
| Run has the role but the latest occurrence is a different stage name | Bound to that occurrence, as today (`latestStageForRole` is role-based). |
| Same-name recapture with identical bytes | Valid append; gate binds to the new occurrence with the same digest. Ambiguity of producer metadata is pre-existing. |
| Historical gate cites a digest no longer on the newest same-name stage | Validates against the earlier occurrence. |
| Historical gate cites a digest on no same-name occurrence | Rejected, unchanged behaviour. |
| Empty artifact file | Rejected by the CLI before the engine, unchanged. |

